WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.080
Every tax season, a CA firm types the same figures again and again: the client's Tally export, the 26AS, AIS and TIS, and then the official utility, by hand.

2
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:26.640
SimplyFile takes the client's books in, maps every figure, reconciles it with the portal, computes the tax, and fills the department's own format, ready for the partner to sign.

3
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:39.390
Upload the client's statement straight from Excel. SimplyFile has already suggested where almost every row belongs. Accept them all in one click.

4
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:53.820
Then the books against the portal, deductor by deductor. One red: the books claim more TDS than the 26AS shows. Explain it, and the year moves on by itself.

5
00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:07.220
The computation, the ITR JSON and the Form 3CB-3CD, in the income-tax department's own format, each checked against its schema, ready for the partner to sign off.

6
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:19.180
SimplyFile. From the client's Excel to the department's JSON, for your whole practice. Try it live, with a made-up firm, on the demo.
